Down there is Jêrin. It's Feqîran (Poor people's place).

123
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Em çûbûn a wê gundî gawiran ko me...
 
We went to that Christian village where we...

124
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Ê gawiran wê de dî, Feqîran wê di binî de ye.
 
Yes, the Christians are over there, Feqîran is below it.

125
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Ewa!
 
Exactly!

126
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Ha jî dibêjin, me gote... Erê hevalno, ev der Kefardelê
Jêrin e, wê de jî jêr e, em kê herin wê derê jî wekî
sewirînin.
 
They also say, we said... Yes friends, this place is
Kefardelê Jêrin, over there is down, we will go there too
and film.

127
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Bes em çûbûn gawiran ko, jorîn dî me çûbûn, me reqsek xweş
kir.
 
But we had gone to the Christian village, the upper one, we
danced nicely.

128
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Mezinên gawiran... koça wan çûna ecêb.
 
The elders of the Christians... their migration is strange.

129
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Erê em li wê derê... Me nizanibû ev...
 
Yes, we were there... We didn't know this...

130
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Tûtîya wa qurtê wa.
 
Their mulberries, their places.

131
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Maşallah, mintiqek mezin e. Ê li piştê tilê da ye, me got em
ê ber wê werin derbas bikin... têr da qed... we re em ê
nêzîk e.
 
Mashallah, it's a large area. It's behind the hill, we said
we would pass by it... since it's very close.

132
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Ehlê we sax be. Gundê me hatin e we, cihê we, Xwedê Xwedê...
Siheta we xweş.
 
Bless your family. You have come to our village, your place,
God God... Bless you.

133
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:59,000
Siheta te xweş. Xalo kasî di te de heye şebab me bab?
 
Bless you. Uncle, do you have any young people here?

134
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Wella we.. silavê min...
 
Well... my greetings...

135
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Silavê xwo bêje. Ka te ser kin. Gulek!
 
Give your greetings. Look here. Say a word!

136
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Pêşî da min bi te re... Ê we be lê... me jî be lê... Xwedê
starê xelqê ke.
 
First of all, with you... Yes... us too... May God protect
the people.

137
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Xwedê xweşiyê bide, xêrê xweşiyê da be. Û çi qas hevalên me
û miletê me yê kurd, gişt xweşiyê da be, gişt..
 
May God grant happiness, may goodness be in happiness. And
all our friends and our Kurdish nation, may they all be in
happiness, all..

138
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Amîn. Amîn.
 
Amen. Amen.

139
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Silavê min ji miletê gundê Gazê re hene, çavê giya maç
dikim. Çûçek û mezin, Xwedê we giya biparêze, gundekî wek
kîbar û xweş.
 
I have greetings for the people of Gazê village, I kiss
everyone's eyes. Small and big, may God protect you all, a
village so elegant and beautiful.

140
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Wekî apê Azad rûniştîk apê xweş!
 
Like uncle Azad sitting, a good uncle!

141
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Ha ha.
 
Ha ha.

142
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Biniya çekçeko ne we xalo?
 
The bottom of the tree is nice, isn't it, uncle?

143
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,000
Wê çendê... hewşê we.
 
That's it... your yard.

144
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Mintaqê xweş e ha.
 
It's a nice area.

145
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,000
E badînê û.. miletê badîno jî pir av e jî... dîme.
 
And Badînê and... the people of Badîno also have a lot of
water... I saw it.

146
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Ne we xalo... Am giha yek in ha.. me ji hevdu birrî, am êdî
hev ne.. Wa noko ev rê ya wî derê, we gundî yê me rast mî
wa?
 
Isn't it, uncle... We are all one.. we have cut ties with
each other, we are no longer together.. Look, now this road
there, is this village really ours?

147
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Kulfetê me, ji eyala we ye.
 
Our family, they are your relatives.

148
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Êê maşallah.
 
Ehh mashallah.

149
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Xalo vê gundê çiqas hewşê heye?
 
Uncle, how many houses are there in this village?

150
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Teqrîben 40-50 mal.
 
Approximately 40-50 houses.

151
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Ehh, dora 40-50 malê heye ne?
 
Ehh, around 40-50 houses, right?

152
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Ev deverê wan a, ev reka darê ye, ev destê gund re ye.
Defterekî heye.
 
This area of theirs, this line of trees, this is the
beginning of the village. There is a notebook.

153
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
Xalo hun tabî'a kîderê ne?
 
Uncle, where are you affiliated with?

154
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Em tabî'a Efrînê ne.
 
We are affiliated with Efrîn.

155
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Hûn ne tabî'a Mabatayê deran ne?
 
Aren't you affiliated with Mabata?

156
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Na em Efrînê, rasterast me Mabatê ye.
 
No, we are Efrîn, directly with Mabata.

157
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,000
Mobaşere Efrîn e?
 
Directly Efrîn?

158
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,000
Mobaşere yê Efrîn e.
 
Directly Efrîn.

159
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
Xalo, kerbê dewletê ne gihîştî gundê we ha na?
 
Uncle, the state's electricity hasn't reached your village,
has it?

160
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,000
Ceryan î nehatîye gund ma.
 
Electricity hasn't come to our village.

161
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Ê we am pîr in ha?
 
And we are old, huh?

162
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Em pîr in, em pîr in.
 
We are old, we are old.

163
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Lwêha tavê, rwêha tavê.
 
Solar panels, solar panels.

164
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Tab, xalo, av gund da heye, şixolê xezano heye?
 
OK, uncle, is there water in the village, do the tanks work?

165
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Av şixolê.. av heye.
 
Water works.. there is water.

166
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Yanî niha belav dibe?
 
I mean, is it distributed now?

167
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:28,000
Belav dibe heftê dû cara, carekî derdixe, carekî ne derdixe,
yanî mecbûrî derdixe.
 
It's distributed twice a week, once it comes out, once it
doesn't, meaning it comes out necessarily.

168
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:32,000
Rind e, wela ew rind in hema.
 
That's good, by God that's good.

169
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Ew hene xezan, em jê radikin.
 
Those tanks are there, we pump from them.

170
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Rind e, xwezî av hebe. Yanî heftê carekî, sîtêlek te jî
werin?
 
Good, I wish there was water. I mean once a week, do your
buckets come too?

171
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,000
Ee taqrîben sîtêlek weh.
 
Yes, approximately a bucket.

172
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,000
Hema rind, heftê stêlek xanî... mehê...
 
That's good, a bucket a week for a house... a month...

173
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
De saet sê saet tê em tijî dikin.
 
It comes for three hours, we fill it.

174
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
Rind e, nola malê.. nola malê maşellah ketime...
 
It's good, like a house... like a house, mashallah I got
into...

175
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Maşellah per gundê me da heye ev şixule, ev xezan.
 
Mashallah, this work, these tanks are everywhere in our
village.

176
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Ê, xalo, vêra me gundî mazên in. Ev Kefardelê... Do we xarê
jî?
 
Yeah, uncle, we have big villages around here. This
Kefardelê... Are they down below too?

177
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:56,000
Ew wê de wê, ev kefardelê ye.
 
They are over there, this is Kefardelê.

178
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Maşellah, ev dirêj e. Xalo, eger heftê...
 
Mashallah, it's long. Uncle, if a week...

179
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Eger heftê neqlikek av ware sîtêlek te... yek pêsrafiye xew
pir bê. Û encam, heftê neqlik av xerc dibe? Neqlikek jî 20
bermîlin, na wa e xalo?
 
If a load of water comes a week, your bucket... one advances
their sleep a lot. And as a result, a load of water is
consumed a week? A load is also 20 barrels, isn't it, uncle?

180
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Wê bi ceryan e jî di saetê de, di saetê de ew we digrin jê,
tê de tijî dikin ew we baranê... ew we di wê de ferq e.
 
It's also with electricity in an hour, in an hour they get
it from it, they fill it in it, that rain... that is
different in it.

181
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:16,000
Xalo, em li hewşê van gundana derî ne.. wa hewşan kevnar
in.. Emrê...
 
Uncle, we are going out of the yards of these villages..
these yards are old.. The age...

182
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Hemû kevnar in. Ewe tabe... ev tabe... Ewe emrê vê gundî...
 
They are all old. That floor... this floor... This is the
age of this village...

183
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Emrê vê gundî bo xalo teqrîben çend sal e? Gor.. gor ti
zani?
 
How many years is the age of this village, uncle,
approximately? As... as far as you know?

184
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Welle ez nizanim. Pirsîm mezinan... emrê min di nav 65-66 da
ye.
 
I swear I don't know. I asked the elders... my age is around
65-66.

185
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

186
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:39,000
Bavê min weha mezin bûye, ez wisa... bavê min got ez weha
mezin bûye.. min got...
 
My father grew up like this, I... my father said I grew up
like this.. I said...

187
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Tu çend bavan nas dikî? Te bîr ê te çend bav e?
 
How many generations do you know? How many generations do
you remember?

188
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:45,000
Welle min gihaye yekê. Lê bavê xwe dît.
 
Well, I reached one. But I saw my father.

189
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,000
Bavê xwe.
 
Your father.

190
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Tu gihayê bavê xwe.
 
You reached your father.

191
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,000
Te nediye...
 
You didn't see...

192
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Maşallah, gundekî kevnar e. Bêşekî 'ewim, gundî me Kurmanca
gelek 500 salin e, na neha?
 
Mashallah, it's an old village. Generally, our Kurmanji
village is around 500 years old, isn't it now?

193
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:58,000
Cemîl wek ko kuleh xwe sêwirî, xwe çêker.
 
Cemil, as if he imagined his hat, built it himself.

194
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Xweda rehma xwe lêke.
 
May God have mercy on him.

195
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
Xweda rehmê...
 
May God have mercy...

196
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Xweda rehma xwe lêke... Wela gundekî pir xweş e. Xwasa bi ev
berke.. ev xwarê ev...
 
May God have mercy on him... By God, it's a very beautiful
village. Especially this pool.. this bottom one...

197
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Êê barko ji betun kirine...
 
Yes, they made the pool out of concrete...

198
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Wa ye, bînî me... ba... balê dixwe.. binê ser zer e ew a tê
mera. Bînî qa lemuye binê darên senoqer e? Xweş e, mintiqek
pir xweş e.
 
Yes, underneath us... it blows.. its bottom is yellow, that
comes to us. Is it underneath the lemon tree or the pine
trees? It's nice, it's a very nice area.

199
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Raste qada we raste.
 
True, your space is true.

200
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Welle, maşallah xweş e kîbar e. Mê gote miletê Gazê lê
sêrkira û te'lîqan per xwe ji me re şikir.
 
I swear, mashallah it's beautiful and elegant. The people of
Gazê said they watched it and thanked us a lot for the
comments.

201
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Loyî milca we re ye? Badîn e.
 
Is it your shelter? Badîn is.

202
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,000
Kî ji wa we?
 
Which one of them?

203
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Azad.. milê.. Ehmedî... Hesênî... Xelk kî ra ye?
 
Azad.. the side.. Ehmedî... Hesênî... Where are the people
from?

204
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Azad, Loyê te... E.. Cîranê min in a...
 
Azad, your Loy... E.. They are my neighbors...

205
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Azad, Lo Hanîf, erê erê...
 
Azad, Lo Hanîf, yes yes...

206
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Êê, Azad! Lo.. ta ye... Cîranê te me. Azad am ê cem kalekî
wane.. am ê cem vir derê rûniştine. Silavê me j' te re hene,
Azad... ev niştek te ha xwar e... cîranê te me. Hehe.
 
Yeah, Azad! Your... Lo... I am your neighbor. Azad, we are
with an old man.. we are sitting here. We have greetings for
you, Azad... you have a seat here... I am your neighbor.
Hehe.

207
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Wele serçavê min... çi sitfe... dîne am hatin.. bavê cîranê
me derket.
 
By God, upon my eyes... what a coincidence... look we came..
the father of our neighbor came out.

208
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Xalo, em we dizanin Azad me ciwan e? Me gote ez û te heval
in.
 
Uncle, we know Azad is young? I said you and I are friends.

209
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
...
 
...

210
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Ser serî me ser çavî me. Kînek xerîb hatî gundê xwedanê
malê?
 
Upon our head, upon our eyes. Has a stranger come to the
village of the house owner?

211
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Ew hatin. Xwedê qebûl bike. Bê guman xelkê me ye.
 
They came. May God accept. Without a doubt, it's our people.

212
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Erê gelê gundî bûn. Bûyer çêbûn gelê wan nexweş bûn. Feqîr û
êşgir hatin. Bûyer çêbûn nexweş ketin.
 
Yes, they were the village people. Incidents happened, their
people got sick. The poor and suffering came. Incidents
happened, they fell ill.

213
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Hêvî dikim xwedê şifayê bide wan.
 
I hope God heals them.

214
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:25,000
Şifayê bide. Şifaya wan bide ji bo xatirê Muhemmed.
 
May He heal. May He heal them for the sake of Muhammad.

215
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Amîn! Me jî negot ya Rebî. Amîn. Welle, niha em hatin komên
xelkê jî li hev in...
 
Amen! We also didn't say, oh Lord. Amen. By God, now we
came, the crowds of people are also together...

216
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:39,000
Keçikên we ye ha. Keçikên we. Kurên we. Silav! Silav! Silav!
Silav! Haha.
 
Your girls. Your girls. Your boys. Hello! Hello! Hello!
Hello! Haha.

217
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
...
 
...

218
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:46,000
Kurdistan, Kurdistan! Xalo, xalo! Kurên te Kurdistan in!
Silav bide, silav bide, silav bide.
 
Kurdistan, Kurdistan! Uncle, uncle! Your sons are Kurdistan!
Greet, greet, greet.

219
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Niha ew keçikê te... keçikê te... pir şirîn e.. wê got.
 
Now that girl of yours... that girl of yours... is very
sweet.. she said.

220
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Xwedê heyê, Xwedê heyê...
 
God exists, God exists...

221
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,000
Cilên we kurmancî ne... wa ye maşallah.
 
Your clothes are Kurmanji... there it is, mashallah.

222
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:59,000
Cilên me kurmancî ne, şalwarê me yek e...
 
Our clothes are Kurmanji, our pants are the same...

223
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:19,000
Welle.. welle. Xwedê te bi hêz bike. Înşeallah tu bi
rihetiyê dijî. Înşeallah! Ne.. Mehdî, Mehdî, ev... Em
rûniştine, ne di cîhê xwe de, ne xizmetek dikim, ne bi xêr
in. Sata te xweş! Xwedê te xweş be. Dembaş, em niha vîdeoyê
qeyd dikin, ez ê pêşkeş bikim, wê hingê derbas bibim... Em ê
bên ba we... Em ê herin...
 
By God.. by God. May God give you strength. Inshallah you
live in peace. Inshallah! No.. Mehdî, Mehdî, this... We are
sitting down, not in our place, not serving, not doing good.
Bless you! May God bless you. Have a good time, we are
recording a video now, I will present it, then I will
pass... We will come to you... We will go...

224
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:46,000
[Music plays]
 
[Music plays]

225
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Ne berf e, ewê dawerivî jî dûr e, digirî.
 
No it's not snow, the dripping is long and round.

226
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Û ew tim bi destan jî têne avakirin kevir.
 
And they are always built by hand with stones.

227
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Çêdikirin... dêr.
 
They used to build... churches.

228
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Û taqên wan jî, ji kevir tim ba dikirin.
 
And their arches, they would always construct from stones.

229
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:14,000
Ba dikirin maneya wê, qişra ji heriyê.
 
"Ba dikirin" means the plaster made of mud.

230
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Yanî bi hevdu re pir alîkarî dikirin, li serî hevdu kom
dibûn.
 
I mean they used to help each other a lot, they would gather
together.

231
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Yanî ne bi pere bûye, yanî berê gund tim alîkariya hevdu
dikirin, diçûn alîkariya hevdu.
 
I mean it wasn't for money, in the past the village always
helped each other, they went to help each other.

232
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:26,000
Yanî wekî niha nizanim dinya çawa bûye.
 
I mean like now, I don't know how the world has become.

233
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Yanî yek wê kevirêkî tayê ane jî, bêrî rake çakûç wê
derkeve, te key pere pe de.
 
I mean if someone just places a stone, picks up a shovel and
a hammer, he will say give me money for it.

234
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Ê çiqas kê ma'îşe çawa tim bûye, feqîre milet rehet e.
 
And no matter how the living conditions always were, the
poor people are relaxed.

235
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,000
Ê çiqas kê ew bûye, anî... na wek berê.
 
And no matter how much it was, it brought... not like the
past.

236
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Berê pir xweş bûye, hezkirin pir bûye.
 
The past was very beautiful, there was a lot of love.

237
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,000
Hevdu re alîkarî dikirin, her tiştkî.
 
They helped each other with everything.

238
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Aha nika jî meselen xanî rabûye, aletê hedîs derketine.
 
Look now for example houses have risen, modern tools have
come out.

239
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:52,000
Evê gelek me ra wekî dibe... a bo tiştê turasî tê hesb.
 
This for many of us becomes like... ah it's considered a
traditional thing.

240
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Gelek me ra çêke, ewê jî hebe.
 
For many of us build it, let it be there.

241
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:59,000
Nika evo sa çêkirî bo te, dît wek berê milat ba wê ana, bi
ro, wext li wext.
 
Now this one made for you here, see like the people in the
past were, day by day, time by time.

242
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:02,000
Bi germî, û berf da anî, ê pir xweş bû.
 
With warmth, and snow brought it, it was very beautiful.

243
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:05,000
Teb'en nika jî tiştê hedîs ev tam tê da nayê.
 
Of course now also modern things don't have this taste.

244
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:09,000
Tiştên kevn wek vî... tişkî têde rehet dibî, pir xweş dibe.
 
Old things like this... you feel relaxed in them, it is very
beautiful.

245
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,000
Maşaellah.
 
Mashallah.

